Compare identical closed-loop nonstreaming synthetic chat calls over direct
HTTP and gateway TLS. Use the real PostgreSQL owner and installed gateway
process fixture. Use 12 warm-up and 96 measured calls for one and two
callers, with one connection per call on both paths. Validate the returned
model and token counts, count all responses, and independently wait for
one exact successful receipt per admitted request. Include capacity refusals
in the offered rate and report success and refusal separately. This is a
single-node synthetic comparison, with the private spool and PostgreSQL
on tmpfs. It uses no model weights or GPU.
